{"name":"Byron Place","hex":"#31667d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"place","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area; somewhere within an area.\nAn open space, particularly a city square, market square, or courtyard.\n\n A street, sometimes but not always surrounding a public place, square, or plaza of the same name.","An open space, particularly a city square, market square, or courtyard."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put (someone or something) in a specific location.","To earn a given spot in a competition; to rank at a certain position ()."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/place"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lord Byron","blocks":[{"text":"George Noel Gordon Byron, 6th Baron Byron, was a British poet. He was one of the major figures of the Romantic movement, and is regarded as being among the greatest British poets. Among his best-known works are the lengthy narratives Don Juan and Childe Harold's Pilgrimage; many of his shorter lyrics in Hebrew Melodies also became popular."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Byron_1813_by_Phillips.jpg/330px-Byron_1813_by_Phillips.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Byron","wikidata":"Q5679"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Autograph-LordByron.png/500px-Autograph-LordByron.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Autograph-LordByron.png/500px-Autograph-LordByron.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAutograph-LordByron.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/CaptainByron.jpg/250px-CaptainByron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.o